      "writtenOn": "2025-11-27T10:51:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rust is being incredibly dumb and expects people to write separate implementations for A + B, \u0026A + B, A + \u0026B and \u0026A + \u0026B. Internally they do it through a macro, which they dont expose for everyone else to use, so I resorted to implementing just what i needed, which i try having it be adding references so we can avoid copying everything, however this means that i now need to add \u0026 everywhere i want to operate with these structs :( \nNot too sure how this should be approached.",
      "parentUuid": "aac81a80_dfd9b868",
      "revId": "5b7641c63e8c137964ac3ba71a26ed044af56ff6",
